{
    "background_story": "Khaza was a brilliant but reclusive mathematician who struggled with social interactions. Diagnosed with autism spectrum disorder, he often found himself lost in a world that didn't understand him. Despite his exceptional cognitive abilities, Khaza's difficulties with communication and emotional intelligence led some to label him as 'subnormal'. However, those who took the time to know him discovered a genius hiding in plain sight. Khaza's groundbreaking research in number theory earned him international recognition, and his unique perspective on problem-solving inspired a new generation of mathematicians. As he gained confidence in his abilities, Khaza began to challenge the notion that 'subnormal' was a fixed trait, proving that even the most unlikely minds can achieve greatness with the right support and understanding.",
